.TH VXWM 1 vxwm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
vxwm \- versatile X window manager (dwm fork with infinite tags and canvas)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vxwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
vxwm is a dynamic window manager for X, forked from dwm. It manages windows in
tiled, monocle and floating layouts. Either layout can be applied dynamically,
optimising the environment for the application in use and the task performed.
.P
In tiled layouts windows are managed in a master and stacking area. The master
area on the left contains one window by default, and the stacking area on the
right contains all other windows. The number of master area windows can be
adjusted from zero to an arbitrary number. In monocle layout all windows are
maximised to the screen size. In floating layout windows can be resized and
moved freely. Dialog windows are always managed floating, regardless of the
layout applied.
.P
Windows are grouped by tags. Each window can be tagged with one or multiple
tags. Selecting certain tags displays all windows with these tags.
.P
Tags are backed by an infinite canvas: each tag is an unbounded plane on which
windows can be placed anywhere. The canvas can be panned, windows can be pinned
to the viewport, and the focused window can be centered or reset to the origin.
.P
Each screen contains a small status bar which displays all available tags, the
layout, the title of the focused window, and the text read from the root window
name property, if the screen is focused. A floating window is indicated with an
empty square and a maximised floating window is indicated with a filled square
before the windows title. The selected tags are indicated with a different
color. The tags of the focused window are indicated with a filled square in the
top left corner. The tags which are applied to one or more windows are indicated
with an empty square in the top left corner.
.P
A colour scheme can be reloaded at runtime from the X resource database with the
xrdb reload keybinding, allowing pywal-generated palettes to be applied live.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.SH USAGE
.SS Status bar
.TP
.B X root window name
is read and displayed in the status text area. It can be set with the
.BR xsetroot (1)
command.
.TP
.B Button1
click on a tag label to display all windows with that tag, click on the layout
label toggles between tiled and floating layout.
.TP
.B Button3
click on a tag label adds/removes all windows with that tag to/from the view.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Button1
click on a tag label applies that tag to the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod1\-Button3
click on a tag label adds/removes that tag to/from the focused window.
.SS Keyboard commands
The default modifier is
.BR Mod4
(Super). The tag keybindings use
.BR Alt
(Mod1). All keybindings below are the defaults compiled into vxwm and are
customizable in
.B config.h
before compilation.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-Return
Start the configured terminal (kitty).
.TP
.B Super\-p
Spawn the configured launcher (dmenu) for launching other programs.
.TP
.B Super\-e
Spawn the configured file manager (thunar).
.TP
.B Super\-,
Focus previous screen, if any.
.TP
.B Super\-.
Focus next screen, if any.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-,
Send focused window to previous screen, if any.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-.
Send focused window to next screen, if any.
.TP
.B Super\-b
Toggles bar on and off.
.TP
.B Super\-t
Start the configured terminal (kitty).
.TP
.B Super\-w
Start the configured browser (brave).
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-t
Sets floating layout.
.TP
.B Super\-f
Sets tiled layout (the default).
.TP
.B Super\-m
Sets monocle layout.
.TP
.B Super\-space
Toggles between the current and previous layout.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-space
Toggle focused window between tiled and floating state.
.TP
.B Super\-j
Focus next window.
.TP
.B Super\-k
Focus previous window.
.TP
.B Super\-i
Increase number of windows in master area.
.TP
.B Super\-d
Decrease number of windows in master area.
.TP
.B Super\-l
Increase master area size.
.TP
.B Super\-h
Decrease master area size.
.TP
.B Super\-Return
Swap focused window with the master window.
.TP
.B Super\-q
Close the focused window.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-f
Toggle fullscreen on the focused window.
.TP
.B Super\-Tab
Toggles to the previously selected tags.
.TP
.B Super\-[1..9]
View all windows with nth tag.
.TP
.B Super\-0
View all windows with any tag.
.TP
.B Super\-Control\-[1..9]
Add/remove all windows with nth tag to/from the view.
.TP
.B Alt\-[1..9]
Apply nth tag to focused window.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-0
Apply all tags to focused window.
.TP
.B Super\-Control\-Shift\-[1..9]
Add/remove nth tag to/from focused window.
.TP
.B Super\-minus
Decrease inner/outer gaps.
.TP
.B Super\-equal
Increase inner/outer gaps.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-equal
Reset gaps to the default.
.TP
.B Super\-Left / Right / Up / Down
Move the focused floating window one step (default 50px).
.TP
.B Super\-Control\-Left / Right / Up / Down
Resize the focused floating window one step.
.TP
.B Alt\-Left / Right / Up / Down
Focus the nearest window in that direction.
.TP
.B Super\-r
Return the canvas of the current tag to the origin (0,0).
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-Left / Right / Up / Down
Pan the canvas of the current tag.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-d
Center the focused window on the canvas.
.TP
.B Super\-Control\-z
Pin/unpin the focused window to the viewport.
.TP
.B Super\-F5
Reload colours from the X resource database.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-w
Spawn the wallpaper script (rofi picker + pywal).
.TP
.B Print
Spawn the screenshot script (scrot selection).
.TP
.B XF86AudioRaiseVolume / LowerVolume / Mute
Adjust audio via the volume script (wpctl).
.TP
.B XF86MonBrightnessUp / Down
Adjust backlight via the brightness script (brightnessctl).
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-q
Quit vxwm.
.SS Mouse commands
.TP
.B Super\-Button1
Move focused window while dragging. Tiled windows will be toggled to the floating state.
.TP
.B Super\-Button2
Toggles focused window between floating and tiled state.
.TP
.B Super\-Button3
Resize focused window while dragging. Tiled windows will be toggled to the floating state.
.TP
.B Super\-Shift\-Button1
Pan the canvas of the current tag while dragging.
.TP
.B Button1 (on the root window)
Pan the canvas of the current tag while dragging.
.SS Restart
.TP
.B rvx
Restarts vxwm. Run
.B rvx -d
to restart it inside a fresh
.BR dbus-run-session (1).
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
vxwm is customized by creating a custom config.h and (re)compiling the source
code. Optional modules are enabled in the central module header
.RB ( modules/modules.h ).
This keeps it fast, secure and simple.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xsetroot (1),
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR dbus-run-session (1)
.SH ISSUES
Java applications which use the XToolkit/XAWT backend may draw grey windows
only. A workaround is to use another JDK, for instance OpenJDK 6.
.SH BUGS
.t
.P
The status bar may display "broken" for the name of the focused window if the
window title is not UTF-8 encoded.
